only if the diff touches hot paths, I/O, loops over unbounded data, locking/concurrency, or startup.\n   Say which optional critics you skipped and why.\n9. Treat findings as hypotheses. Reproduce or reason through every BLOCKER/HIGH, fix every confirmed BLOCKER and HIGH, and fix MEDIUM findings that affect correctness, reliability, security, or likely regressions.\n10. Rerun focused tests first, then the broader suite. Stop when a round produces no NEW confirmed BLOCKER/HIGH findings.\n11. Never make tests pass by weakening assertions, deleting coverage, skipping tests, broadening mocks, or disabling lint/type checks.\n\nFINAL REPORT:\n- Requirements summary\n- Work plan: which worker owned which file scope\n- Per-worker results, including anything left undone or reported out of scope\n- Validation commands actually run and results\n- Critics run/skipped, findings by category, findings fixed vs rejected with reasons\n- Remaining limitations or environment failures\n- Exact final test/build status"
